From e2ef42b5e8eee1b5307ea48d6c312f9449dfae7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:50:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] n-gram table: --ngram-table ram reads it from a locked
 copy in RAM

embed_lookup_q reads the n-gram table through a row cache and direct reads,
and about half of a step's rows are first-seen, so steps wait on the drive.
--ngram-table ram (default disk, unchanged) copies the table into locked
huge pages in the background, checks the copy against the mapping and then
serves the gather from memory. MemAvailable, RLIMIT_MEMLOCK and the cgroup
limit are checked first; if any is short the table stays on disk. The flag
reaches the plugin as an optional `resident` parameter of embed_lookup_q.
